3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT

No permission for Commercial Use is granted by this license. You must obtain
prior written consent from zemw, the project author, under separately agreed
terms before any Commercial Use of the Covered Work. Publishing source code,
providing attribution, or receiving a copy from another person does not replace
that consent. Silence or failure to enforce is not consent. Separate permission
applies only to the parties, work, uses, and duration it expressly covers.
The author may grant permissions only for rights the author owns or is authorized
to license; separate third-party permissions may also be necessary.

4. SOURCE SHARING WHEN DISTRIBUTING

Whenever you give another person a copy of a Covered Work, whether as source,
compiled code, a browser application, an installer, or another form, you must:

(a) provide that recipient the complete Corresponding Source, at no charge,
    either with the copy or through a clearly identified download link accessible
    without a paid subscription or a separate confidentiality agreement;
(b) license your contributions to the Covered Work under this same license,
    and provide a copy of this license with the work and its source;
(c) preserve copyright, attribution, license, and disclaimer notices, and clearly
    identify your modifications and their dates; and
(d) impose no additional terms or technical restrictions that prevent recipients
    from exercising the rights this license grants.

If you use a download link, maintain source access for at least three years
after your last distribution of that version. Provide source for the actual
version distributed; an unrelated or outdated upstream repository is insufficient.
An unmodified version may link to the exact upstream source revision if it
satisfies these requirements; you remain responsible for source availability.

5. SOURCE SHARING FOR NETWORK SERVICES

If you operate a Covered Work so that other people can interact with it remotely
over a network, you must prominently offer those users a clearly labeled,
no-charge link to the complete Corresponding Source of the version in operation,
under this same license. Make the offer visible in the user interface, or in
service documentation for an interface without a visual UI. The offer and source
must remain available throughout operation and for at least three years after
that version was last offered to users. This applies to unmodified as well as
modified versions and applies even when no executable is distributed.

6. PRIVATE USE AND SCOPE

Purely private Noncommercial Use and modifications do not require publication
when you neither distribute copies nor allow other people to interact remotely
with the Covered Work. Distribution triggers section 4; remote use by others
triggers section 5. The source-sharing obligations cover the complete Covered
Work as defined in section 1, not unrelated independent projects or personal data.
Sharing source never authorizes Commercial Use.

Independently licensed third-party material retains its own license. This license
does not grant rights to relicense such material or waive its conditions. You may
combine material only when you can satisfy all applicable licenses; in particular,
you may not assume this license is compatible with GPL or AGPL components.

7. DOWNSTREAM RIGHTS AND CONTRIBUTIONS

Recipients receive permissions for the original Software directly from its
copyright holders under this license; you may not grant broader rights to it.
Your contributions to a distributed or network-accessible Covered Work must be
available under this license, without preventing you from separately licensing
code you independently own, subject to the rights of other copyright holders.

If you intentionally submit a contribution for inclusion in the official TigerAI
project, you represent that you have the right to do so. Unless separately agreed
in writing, you license that contribution under this license and also grant zemw
a perpetual, worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free right to use, modify,
distribute, sublicense, and commercially license it. You retain your copyright.
This additional grant applies to intentionally submitted project contributions,
not automatically to independent forks or their unsubmitted modifications.

8. TERMINATION AND CURE

If you violate this license, the permissions it grants terminate automatically.
For a first violation, they are reinstated if you completely cure it within
30 days after receiving written notice from a copyright holder. Subsequent
violations require express reinstatement by the affected copyright holder.
Reinstatement does not erase liability for prior unauthorized use. Termination
of your rights does not terminate the rights of recipients who remain compliant.

